                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2aabf543-eeb8-457b-bd3e-b4055c184180",
                                "sense_id": "53f1b3e3-6fe2-375a-aa33-54b6a450bdeb",
                                "text": "In de Officiis, Isidore described laudes as an alleluiatic chant."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "33e050f0-19f3-4e3d-950f-7ab9aaaea5e4",
                                "sense_id": "53f1b3e3-6fe2-375a-aa33-54b6a450bdeb",
                                "text": "Evidence of the alleluiatic psalm is found as early as Tertullian (d. 220) and in the contemporary Apostolic Tradition of Hippolytus; as we have seen, it consisted of an acclamation (alleluia) after each verse chanted by a soloist."
                            }
